  "blocks": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "How do you know when a piece of chicken is cooked? Most people think they can "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "tell",
      "ref": "v-tell"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " by the colour. But according to scientific research, that doesn’t always work."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Chicken is among the "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "riskiest",
      "ref": "v-risky"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " foods for "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "Salmonella",
      "zh": "沙门氏菌"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " and "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "Campylobacter",
      "zh": "弯曲杆菌"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ", two of the leading causes of "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "foodborne",
      "zh": "食源性的"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " illness. They can be found "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b1",
      "number": 1
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " chicken meat. That’s why chicken, "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b2",
      "number": 2
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " beef, must be cooked through."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Chicken contains less "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "myoglobin",
      "zh": "肌红蛋白"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " than other meats. As a result, the colour change in the cooking "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b3",
      "number": 3
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " is less noticeable. Recent research shows that it can occur before Salmonella and Campylobacter are "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b4",
      "number": 4
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " killed."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "According to the World Health Organisation, chicken should be cooked to 70 degrees "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "Celsius",
      "zh": "摄氏度"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " to be "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b5",
      "number": 5
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ". But in their research, "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "Norwegian",
      "zh": "挪威的"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " scientist Solveig Langsrud and her team found that most of the colour change happened "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b6",
      "number": 6
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " 55 degrees Celsius."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Using a kitchen thermometer can help make sure that food is safe to eat. But there are problems with this "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b7",
      "number": 7
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ", too. Langsrud and her team tested five thermometers on the market. All but the cheapest were accurate. But even the more expensive ones took up to 15 seconds to give an accurate "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "reading",
      "ref": "v-reading"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ". You also have to test the meat in "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b8",
      "number": 8
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " places to make sure you have found the coldest part."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p6",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Worryingly, even when the "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "core",
      "ref": "v-core"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " of a piece of chicken reached 70 degrees Celsius, Salmonella and Campylobacter could still be found on the "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b9",
      "number": 9
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ". Langsrud suggests that people always cook a piece of chicken on all sides or in a soup. “I would guess that most of the time when people get sick, it’s because they’re eating something that’s "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b10",
      "number": 10
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "raw",
      "zh": "生的"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ",” she says."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
